<title>UK: Saudi tells OPEC it pumped 8.009 mbpd in March.</title>
<headline>Saudi tells OPEC it pumped 8.009 mbpd in March.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia told OPEC it produced 8.009 million barrels a day (bpd) in March, in line with its OPEC quota and unchanged from February, the OPEC news agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The data were submitted directly to OPEC headquarters in Vienna.</p>
<p>Among other submissions Venezuela said it pumped 2.407 million bpd.</p>
<p>Supply as defined by OPEC is calculated as domestic consumption, plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for March so far are as follows:  </p>
<p>		  PRODUCTION     SUPPLY</p>
<p>    Algeria   0.793	    0.777</p>
<p>    Indonesia 1.3267</p>
<p>    Kuwait    2.0095	   2.008</p>
<p>    Libya     1.3920	   1.3970</p>
<p>    Qatar     0.4093</p>
<p>    Saudi     8.0087	   8.0045</p>
<p>    Venezuela 2.4070</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
